    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d549">

                <pb facs="0726" n="440" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg440"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/9736</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-09-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 6, 1916, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 5 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4848. Your 3741,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d549-f1"/> August 25. Foreign Office refers
                    to its note of the 31st, cabled in my 4815 [4814], September 1 and states that
                    bunkers have now been granted the <hi rendition="#italic">Charlton Hall</hi>
                    which is reported to have sailed from Colombo on the 26th and the authorities in
                    Egypt have been notified by telegraph in order that, if requested, similar
                    facilities may be assured her on arrival at Suez or Port Said.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
